  {
   "t": "p",
   "text": "Richmond is split into 29 MLS® sub-areas, the neighbourhood boundaries the Greater Vancouver REALTORS® board uses for every listing and sale. From November 2025 to October 22, 2026, 2,106 homes sold across them: 521 houses, 1,095 condos and 462 townhomes and 20 duplexes. The busiest were Brighouse (490), West Cambie (298), Brighouse South (163).",
   "gen": "gvr"
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "text": "By median price, the houses that sold in Seafair were the most expensive of the 21 Richmond neighbourhoods with 10 or more house sales ($2,428,000), and those in Hamilton the least ($1,198,800). For condos, the range ran from $265,000 in South Arm to $675,000 in Steveston South.",
   "gen": "gvr"
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "text": "These are MLS® sub-areas, not the City of Richmond’s planning areas, so a neighbourhood here can be larger or smaller than the name suggests. The map and tables below follow the board’s boundaries. Use them to compare areas, then ask Jared for a search set to the exact streets you care about.",
   "gen": "gvr"
  },
